Backport of upstream dulwich commit 1ca18147a1d03b61c2ae203c46bf0b2a2f5dd421
"submodule: Reject unsafe submodule paths in submodule_update" for
CVE-2026-52726 (GHSA-gfhv-vqv2-4544).

A crafted upstream repository could carry a submodule whose path was
".git/hooks" (or any other path inside .git or above the work tree),
causing the submodule's tree contents to be written there with their
executable bits intact -- dropping a hook that later commands would run.
Submodule paths are now rejected if they are absolute or carry a
component that the configured path validator refuses, and the
submodule's own tree is materialized with the same validator.

Adapted for dulwich 1.0.0:
  - The upstream NEWS hunk is dropped.
  - The stash.py and worktree.py hunks that swap the inline
    protectNTFS/protectHFS if/elif/else block for the new
    get_path_element_validator() helper are re-anchored on the
    post-CVE-2026-42305 form of that block (comment header +
    b"protectNTFS"/True + b"protectHFS"/sys.platform == "darwin"),
    because in this app-patcher chain CVE-2026-42305 is applied first
    and rewrites those lines.
